1. **What is the system ultimately trying to become better at learning?** Choosing which hypotheses are worth testing — improving the research-selection policy so each activation converts into a durable retained/rejected search-policy update rather than opportunistic queue picking.
2. **What currently most constrains useful learning?** Task/strategy choice was opportunistic from a queue, producing near-duplicate MA-crossover experiments (base + 3 rescue variations on the same signal class) instead of crossing the unresolved frontier.
3. **What uncertainty prevents a better decision?** No controlled counterfactual (queue-run without the selector) exists in durable state — the advantage is evidenced by the documented before/after pattern, so its magnitude isn't measured (direction is documented).
